I *do* want to search "for some portion of the mass of "/=/" and then
give up".  Later, the expression searches again for another portion.
It is part of a slow loop.  You are suggesting a style that could
result in a program that might run considerably faster than this one,
but that would also take more computational resources and take much
longer for me to write.  Since this is a `do once' program, I was more
concerned with the time to write it than its slow execution.

